{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqfh9nmj87j","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"FeatureBench ON arm KB is generated with onboard drop-in entry not the probe competence loop","summary":"CORRECTION to note-mqfh3oipxrq (FB-3 worker overstated the blocker). The ON-arm KB blocks for foreign FeatureBench repos CAN be generated: use scripts/onboard.js (the drop-in mine -> learn -> bundle entry), which needs NO authored probes and writes onboard-notes.json directly (so no daemon /search read-back, sidestepping the foreign-workspace concern). The probe requirement and the hard-exit the worker hit are specific to scripts/onboard-loop.js, which is a competence-MEASUREMENT deepening loop, not the KB-block generator. Foreign-repo onboarding is NOT policy-denied — verified end-to-end on cosma-ai-studio (task c0bd3682/13). Clean two-arm mapping that matches implemented code and the runbook's intended ablation ('does the LLM judge step earn its token cost'): ON-plain = onboard.js --skip-learn (raw mined candidates, unvalidated); ON-self-learning = onboard.js full mine->learn (the read-only learner agent validates mined candidates against source, KEPT/REJECTED — the learner IS the self-learning filter). Export each variant's notes JSON to an AGENTS.md block. Pilot manifest (15 instances / 5 repos: pandas, astropy, sphinx, seaborn, sympy) already committed at bench/featurebench-kb (commit f6f8025).","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T17:19:07.483Z","vec":[-0.1142912432551384,-0.024118322879076004,-0.03829766437411308,-0.031109675765037537,0.009922816418111324,-0.03435799852013588,0.025204777717590332,0.014688106253743172,-0.02946857362985611,0.030944304540753365,0.020180340856313705,-0.06652659177780151,0.025788966566324234,-0.033760927617549896,-0.01983814127743244,0.03921110928058624,0.09447745978832245,-0.057903826236724854,-0.025450680404901505,-0.018834436312317848,-0.017352476716041565,-0.04390903189778328,0.05617478862404823,0.028555478900671005,-0.00